      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "You are right about the inner `break` \u2014 it correctly stops after `4`.\n\nThe trace tells a second story: at `return`, `firsts` is `[4]` and **both** loops show `broken: True`. That means a second reached line stopped the outer `row` loop after only its first item, so the second row was never visited.\n\nThink finger-by-finger: which loop does that outer-body `break` belong to?",
      "follow_up": "If that outer break line were never reached, what would the outer loop do after the first row?",
